        Men's blazer sizing typically follows chest measurements, while women's blazer sizing may use numeric sizes (2, 4, 6, etc.) or letter sizes (XS, S, M, L) based on bust measurements. Women's blazers also require consideration of bust, waist, and hip proportions, with different fit silhouettes including regular, petite, and plus-size categories. Our <a href="/grading-service">grading service</a> creates size charts specifically optimized for your target demographic and market. We manufacture both men's and women's blazers with appropriate sizing systems and fit considerations for each gender.
