      <h2 class="section__title">Blazer Manufacturer FAQ</h2>
      
      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the minimum order for custom blazers?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            SDF Clothing offers custom blazer manufacturing with a minimum order of 300 pieces per style. This low MOQ makes our services accessible to startup brands, boutique labels, and businesses launching new blazer lines. We offer flexible size and color breakdowns within the 300 piece minimum, allowing you to test designs and scale gradually. Our 300 piece MOQ is significantly lower than many manufacturers who require 500-1,000 pieces for tailored garments.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the most popular blazer fabric for fashion brands?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Wool and wool-polyester blends are the most popular blazer fabrics for fashion brands. Wool offers natural drape, breathability, and a premium hand feel that elevates garment quality. Wool-polyester blends (typically 70% wool, 30% polyester) provide wool's aesthetic benefits with added durability, wrinkle resistance, and cost efficiency. For summer collections, linen and cotton blends are popular for their lightweight, breathable properties. Velvet and tweed serve specific fashion segments - velvet for evening and occasion wear, tweed for heritage and autumn collections.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What is the difference between fused and canvas blazer construction?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Fused construction uses adhesive to fuse interlining to the fabric, creating structure at lower cost. Fused blazers are affordable and maintain shape well but have less drape and breathability. Half-canvas construction uses a canvas interlining that floats from the chest to the button area, providing better drape and a more natural silhouette. Full-canvas construction uses canvas throughout the jacket front, offering the highest quality drape and longevity but at premium cost. Fused is ideal for budget-friendly fashion, half-canvas for mid-range quality, and full-canvas for bespoke-level garments.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you make blazers in plus sizes?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, SDF Clothing manufactures blazers in plus sizes. We offer inclusive sizing from XS to 5XL, with custom grading services available for brands requiring extended size ranges. Our pattern making and grading capabilities ensure consistent fit across all size categories. We understand that plus-size customers represent a significant market segment, and we help brands serve this audience with properly fitted blazers that don't compromise on style or proportion. Our plus-size clothing manufacturing services include specialized pattern adjustments for larger sizes.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How long does blazer manufacturing take?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Blazer manufacturing typically takes 45-60 days from sample approval to shipment. The timeline includes: pattern making and grading (5-7 days), sample development with all construction details (10-14 days), sample approval and any revisions (3-5 days), cutting and sewing bulk production (25-35 days), final quality inspection and finishing (3-5 days), and packing for shipment (2-3 days). Complex styles with multiple linings, special fabrics, or intricate details may add 5-10 days. Rush orders may be possible at higher cost for time-critical launches.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you make matching blazer and trouser sets?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, SDF Clothing manufactures matching blazer and trouser sets as coordinated suits. We ensure fabric and color consistency across both garments by cutting from the same fabric batch and using identical dye lots. Our pattern making capabilities guarantee matching proportions and styling elements between blazer and trousers. Coordinating sets are popular for corporate uniforms, formal wear collections, and fashion brands offering complete outfit solutions. We also manufacture matching waistcoats for three-piece suit sets.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What certifications do your blazer fabrics have?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            SDF Clothing's blazer fabrics hold multiple international certifications including OEKO-TEX Standard 100 for chemical safety, GOTS for organic cotton options, and REACH compliance for EU markets. Our manufacturing facilities are BSCI certified for social compliance and WRAP certified for ethical manufacturing. These certifications ensure your blazers meet retailer requirements and consumer expectations for safety and responsibility. We provide transaction certificates for certified materials to support your sustainability claims.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">Can you add custom lining with brand print?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Yes, we offer custom lining with brand prints, logos, or patterns. Custom lining is an excellent way to add brand identity to blazers, visible when the garment is worn open. We can print your logo, brand pattern, or custom design on lining fabric using sublimation or screen printing methods. Custom lining works particularly well for corporate blazers, fashion statement pieces, and limited edition collections. We also offer contrasting solid linings in brand colors as a more subtle branding option.
          </p>
        </div>
